/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/sub-step-d-design-iter1.md:305:2. **NEW absorbed (D-3) extends the `git add` + `git commit` to the promote-now path. The hook does not write to git index** — it writes only to `session.json` (a session memory file). So T3 introduces no new git commit; it only adds rows to a single JSON file. The per-iteration session-memory commit (D-4) covers the persistence of those JSON-file changes to the worktree branch. T3's hook does NOT need to trigger a git commit itself; the loop's MEMORIZATION phase commits the rolled-up session-memory delta on exit.
